    "body": "Finding: the fix needs golden changes. I stop here and do not regenerate goldens.\n\nCause:\n- `arc_over` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/arcs.rs` lets each vertex stand up to `tol * ARC_FIT_VERTEX_SHARE` (0.05 mm at tolerance 0.1) off the fitted circle, on both sides.\n- The verifier allows only `GOUGE_TOL = 0.01` mm (`crates/app/src/operation/material.rs`). It does not use the operation tolerance.\n- Thus an arc can pass a vertex on the part side by more than 0.01 mm. Verify then flags `Gouge` and holds the post.\n\nHeld work: branch `issue/1579-arc-fit-one-sided`, commit af47a6ea8 (pushed, no PR).\n- New `crates/motion/src/machining2d/arc_side.rs`. The circle keeps the end vertices of the run. Its centre moves along their bisector until no interior vertex is on the part side.\n- New `fit_arcs_sided(pts, tol, air_left)`. Contour, contour chain and the lead reseat use it.\n- New pinning test `contour_arc_fit_wall::coarse_arc_fit_on_a_round_wall_verifies_clean_both_ways`. It fails on main (`climb=true`: `Gouge { at: 3 }` ... `Gouge { at: 11 }`) and passes with the fix.\n- New unit test `arcs::a_sided_fit_never_passes_a_vertex_on_the_part_side`. It passes.\n\nQuick gate: the motion suites pass. These app tests fail because the output changes:\n- `arc_entry::contour_bore_arc_entry_matches_golden`\n- `golden_cl::contour_disc_hole_matches_golden`\n- `golden_cl::contour_tangential_lead_matches_golden`\n- `solid_law_goldens::every_depth_law_golden_verifies_exactly_as_before`\n- `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes`\n- `solid_law_goldens::a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused` (the Crossing move indices change)\n- `thread_boss::an_external_m8_thread_verifies_clean_and_posts_helical_moves` (Rough1 posts two arcs and a line, not three arcs)\n\nReason: a closed ring on an inside wall (a hole, a bore) and the M8 boss now fail the air-side check (slack 1e-9). The ring then falls back to an open run and a line. These goldens had exact circles (`I20000 J10000`), so the check is too strict for vertex noise on a true circle.\n\nNext step options:\n1. Give the closed-ring check a slack near `GOUGE_TOL` and constrain only the vertices past that slack. This can keep the goldens unchanged.\n2. Accept the new output and regenerate the goldens. This needs a decision by the maintainer.\n\nI release the claim. The effort label stays `effort:high`.\n",
